"/athletes/72305"} "Herb McKenley"] " received the baton for his third leg, he was over 10 metres in arrears. Racing against " [:a {:href "/results/58950"} "400 hurdles"] " gold medalist " [:a {:href "/athletes/78806"} "Charlie Moore"] ", McKenley ran the fastest 400 leg yet recorded, 44.6 – the first time any runner had bettered 45 seconds for 400 metres. As they neared the bell lap, McKenley gave Jamaica a narrow lead. The anchor was contested between Jamaica’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/72324"} "George Rhoden"] " and the USA’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/79185"} "Mal Whitfield"] ", who had won the " [:a {:href "/results/58880"} "400"] " and " [:a {:href "/results/58903"} "800 metre"] " gold medals, respectively. Whitfield ran on Rhoden’s shoulder for the entire last lap, but could never quite pull even or pass him. Jamaica won the gold medal in the greatest 4x400 relay to that time, breaking the world record, with the United States also bettering the old mark, by over four seconds."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitors"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "R1"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "–"] [:td {} "Jamaica"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/JAM"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/JAM.png"}] "JAM"]] [:td {} "3:12.1 (1 h1)"] [:td {} "3:03.9 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "label label-default"} [:abbrev {:title "World Record"} "WR"]]] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {}] [:td {}] [:td {:colspan "10"} [:a {:href "/athletes/72341"} "Arthur Wint"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/72300"} "Les Laing"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/72305"} "Herb McKenley"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/72324"} "George Rhoden"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/72299"} "Byron LaBeach"] [:small {} " (DNS)"]]] [:tr {:clas